{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin","id":387978,"title":"Dark Eras: Cold War Berlin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-31T21:18:17-08:00","id":387978,"title":"Dark Eras: Cold War Berlin","content":"I just read the Dark Eras KS preview. No surprise that Berlin during the frostiest part of the Cold War is a shoo-in, and there\u2019s a lot to like.<br /> <br /> The connection between the G-M and the Loyalists of Thule is brilliant from a story-teller perspective. Unlike the primary anti-demon Hunter faction, the Knights of St. Adrian, the Loyalist are scholars, researchers and nobody\u2019s dupes (well\u2026 depending on your chronicle\u2026). They have a vast store of occult knowledge, including the basics of occult engineering, putting them on the short list of Hunters who are even remotely equipped to handle Infrastructure or Facilities. They operate in much the same manner as Demons do and that makes them brilliant foils.<br /> <br /> The Loyalist could be allies, of opportunity or convenience if not ideology, to the Unchained. G-M designs and misinformation setup the disaster in 1933, so the Loyalists have a common adversary, <i>if</i> they can be convinced that there is a distinction between the Unchained and their former master. Additionally, an Unchained could sign onto the Loyalists\u2019 vision of Thule, as their personal version of Hell. The Loyalists already have the blueprints, saving the Unchained enormous effort\u2026 if they just make sure it\u2019s free of the G-M\u2019s influence this time around.<br /> Other things I like: listing other RPGs in the inspirational materials. Onyx Path has done this before and other RPG lines are doing it was well, but I\u2019m glad to see more and more cross-pollination in the industry.<br /> <br /> As excited as I am about the Thule connection, I have concerns. The What Has Come Before establishes that a G-M plot started a chain of events that lead to one of the darkest eras (heh) in human history by manipulating the organization that would become the Hunter compact, the Loyalists of Thule. The Loyalist involvement with the Nazi party is established canon on the nWoD, but including an overtly supernatural element like G-M to the Holocaust, even as an indirect actor, is risky territory.<br /> <br /> The Holocaust is still remembered by hundreds of thousands of survivors, many more lost friends and family members in the Second World War. Any and all of whom might take serious offense at the notion that these death were somehow an occult or conspiratorial event. Kenneth Hite wrote a killer essay for Achtung Cthulhu about this risk, some of which he discusses online here (<a href=\"http://frabjousdave.com/creative-colleagues-kenneth-hite/\" target=\"_blank\">http://frabjousdave.com/creative-col...-kenneth-hite/</a>). A line of special importance: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cSuddenly their 20 million victims weren\u2019t murdered by humans, but instead were killed by a freak amoral accident, or died of a plague spread by orcs.\u201d It becomes a tragedy, not a sin. </div> </div> </div> The Loyalists of Thule are humans making human decisions with horrifying consequences, so their previously established involvement doesn\u2019t ping my radar as much. Also, the writing team avoids of absolving mortal responsibility in the matter, which I appreciate.<br /> <br /> Some things that I hope to see:<br /> <br /> <b>A Rashomon with the Widdershins Windmill.</b> As is, we\u2019re told explicitly that it was a G-M plot. A situation were any and every faction might responsible gives an over-arcing mystery to investigate, one that every party has a stake in (\u201cThe Widdershins Windmill was a Saboteur plot that went array and started this entire mess.\u201d \u201cI have verified and credible reports that the Integrators were trying to perform a hard reset of the G-M, try and fix the errors in it\u2019s programming. Went completely south.\u201d \u201cYou\u2019re both wrong, an Exile was trying to get instructions from the Machine. It worked.\u201d \u201cI\u2019ve read the Oera Linda Book, all four translations, there's <i>no</i> sign of God Machine interference or involvement\u201d) Give the setting a murky past to complement the unstable present and the looming future threat of nuclear war. It would also defuse some of my concerns with the Nazis + Supernatural tropes.<br /> <br /> <b>More Uncertainty and Paranoia.</b> \u201cAssume Nothing\u201d is a credo that resonates with both the setting of DtD and the Cold War. Mix them together and you should get a wilderness of mirrors where even reality itself cannot be trusted.<br /> <br /> <b>More Weird.</b> Much of the real world information can be obtained on Wikipedia or in any number of novels or history books. Historical information isn\u2019t as interesting or as useful to me as game information and systems are. The vignettes of little bits of strangeness included in each section is pure gold and I want more. What did World of Darkness Cold War looked like? What plots involving the G-m and other beasties looks like? In short, if I can run a bog standard nWoD game with ordinary mortals (not Hunters) confronting unique supernatural horrors in the Cold War, I\u2019ll consider this section an unqualified and total success.<br /> <br /> <b>Splinters and Nuclear Scenarios.</b> Great thing about Demon the Descent? Time travel and alternate time lines. If the G-M wants to nuke a city, or the entire world, it <i>damn well can</i> and to hell with \u201cestablished history\u201d. The players can screw up, turn the Cold War hot, and have front row seats as Berlin becomes a sea of glowing ash.<br /> <br /> Then the Machine steps in.<br /> <br /> Maybe everyone is recreated by the G-M, including the players\u2019 Covers. Now a real, flesh-and-blood, vanilla mortal is running around thinking he\u2019s the person a Cover pretends to be (Compromise ho!).<br /> <br /> Maybe the G-M creates and repopulates the earth with a completely new batch of people who have no memory of the destroyed world (your mortal friends and family? All dead. Don\u2019t worry though, the G-M has graciously provided replacements). They all have complete histories and memories. They all believe that they existed for their entire lives. They forget the nightmares when the wake up.<br /> <br /> Maybe the G-M can reset the last four days and send a hunter angel after whoever cause the problem (the PCs, because they caused it. They wanted an extra beat so they traded a failure for a dramatic failure during ) the characters now have to correct their mistake while trying to avoid the angel homing in on them. The possibilities are endless, and horrifying. <br /> <br /> <b>The Loyalists of Thule</b> recruited, sometimes forcefully, into the the US, UK and USSR intelligence apparatuses, a la Operation Paperclip. They\u2019re too useful as antagonists, allies and foils. Give the Loyalists access to CIA/Mi-6/KGB resources, send them out against the G-M and Unchained alike, then watch the sparks fly.<br /> <br /> <b>More Cryptids! </b>The Reptilians are perfect for this setting, and desirable mercenaries/slaves/victims to all sides.<br /> <br /> <b>More Sleepers!</b> If there was ever a time when Sleeper agents could cause a demon nightmares, it\u2019s here.<br /> <br /> For the approval of the forum community I submit more resources and inspiration: The Spy Museum Podcast has a number of great episodes for this Era, Ghost Projeckt by Joe Harris and Steve Rolston is not set in the Cold War, or even Berlin, but deals with the legacy of a Cold War attempt to weaponize the supernatural and the atmosphere oozes World of Darkness. Queen and Country: Declassified Vol 1. by Greg Rucka tells the story of a border extraction gone horribly wrong. Cold War Memories: A Retrospective on Living in Berlin: A City Divided--Memoirs of U.S. Dependents in Berlin has great information about living in Berlin during the period, and Black Market, Cold War: Everyday Life in Berlin, 1946-1949 by Paul Steege gives high-level detail on how post-war Berlin became Cold War Berlin.<br /> <br /> Ms. Bailey, Mr. Zawadzki, thank you both, and before you go to bed tonight, please watch:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/x1kwz5u_the-war-game-peter-watkins-1965_tv\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/x1kwz5u_the-war-game-peter-watkins-1965_tv\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/x1kwz5u_the-war-game-peter-watkins-1965_tv\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.dailymotion.com/video/x1kwz5u_the-war-game-peter-watkins-1965_tv </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/5734957/protect-and-survive-nuclear-war-videos-are-chilling-in-their-mundanity/\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/5734957/protect-and-s...eir-mundanity/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T22:49:29-08:00","id":388025,"title":"","content":"I absolutely adore the setting. I fucking hate that they wrote the God-Machine as being behind the rise of the Nazi Party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:19:38-08:00","id":388056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=388025#post388025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely adore the setting. I fucking hate that they wrote the God-Machine as being behind the rise of the Nazi Party.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't, unless you feel like arguing a failure of foresight and human-understanding on the part of an intermediary constitutes ultimate responsibility, or that a single cult's focus on blood-purity was the sole deciding factor in the series of events that led post-WWI Germany to become Nazi Germany, but &quot;Massive Supernatural Operation Had Some Influence on Historical Macroevent Due to Cultist Misunderstanding&quot; is not exactly a groundbreaking secret headline in the scheme of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T00:27:22-08:00","id":388098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=388025#post388025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely adore the setting. I fucking hate that they wrote the God-Machine as being behind the rise of the Nazi Party.</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine was not behind the rise of the Nazi Party. It was only one of many factors, and I'm sorry if that did come across for you in the text. Think of it this way:<br /> <br /> There's this bit in Le Morte d'Arthur wherein the forces of Arthur and of Mordred meet under a flag of truce to discuss a possible peace. During those tense moments one of the knights drew a sword to kill an adder that might otherwise have bitten him. All the enemy knights regarded this as a declaration of war, and so a battle was wrested from the jaws of peace. You can interpret this as a tragedy brought on by a single man's ill-considered actions (which it also is), but what it really shows is just how tightly wound everyone there was. If it hadn't been an adder it might have been an arrow accidentally let loose from bowstring or a horse that got spooked and charged toward the enemy line or any of a thousand other innocuous events that could be misconstrued as open hostility. Even if the troops didn't make any mistakes, those negotiating peace might have failed to reach any agreement, and the battle would have happened anyway.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that the God-Machine knew that one specific knight loyal to Mordred (call him Sir Matt) needed to die in order to complete a key piece of Infrastructure. It doesn't care about Arthur or Mordred or anyone else for that matter. As long Sir Matt lives, the occult matrix will never be complete. The God-Machine runs the numbers, analyzes its options, and seeks a way to off Sir Matt while expending as few of its resources as possible. The war between Arthur and Mordred is already underway. The king has already driven Lancelot out of Camelot, and maybe some of Arthur's knights aren't too happy about it and would turn against the king if not for this immediate problem of a red hot civil war. The Machine doesn't pay close attention to all that background, though. It simply becomes aware that Sir Matt is on the front lines of one of two armies facing each other on opposite sides of a battlefield, and according to its calculations Sir Matt has a 99% chance of dying in any battle that unfolds that day. So it sends an angel in the body of an adder to startle one of the knights - it doesn't matter which one. Sir Matt dies in the resulting melee, and the fact that Mordred dies and Arthur is fatally wounded and all of Camelot collapses in the aftermath of the battle is purely incidental to the God-Machine's plan.<br /> <br /> Is the God-Machine then responsible for the fall of Camelot? Kind of yes but mostly no. Camelot was on death's door. The fact that Mordred's open rebellion had been so successful to that point makes that pretty clear. The battle wasn't inevitable per se, but it was was very nearly unavoidable, and a treaty forged on that battlefield probably would not have changed the outcome (Camelot's fall and Arthur's death) in the long term.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, the God-Machine did not create the Nazis. It didn't create the economic hardships and demographic pressures that made fascism so appealing to a sufficiently large and influential percentage of Germans. Saboteur paranoia to the contrary, It certainly didn't establish death camps or order the firebombing of Dresden or trick Hitler into invading Russia. Humans did all those things on their own and in response to their own hopes, fears, and prejudices. Herr Arger's message was meant to inspire the Thule Society to build a piece of Infrastructure and to protect it as though it were their only hope of escape from a really shitty time and place to be living in. He didn't tell them why they were chosen or how they could prove themselves. That came from the Thule Society, and they did some undeniably shitty things in an effort to convince some assholes in a shining city to take them away from it all.<br /> <br /> Would the Nazis have risen to power without the support of the Thule Society? Quite possibly - and if not them, another group like them. I don't want to go all deterministic, though. I'll allow that maybe it wouldn't have gone down that way at all. Maybe Germany would have limped along for ten or twenty or thirty more years and nothing as terrible as World War II would have taken place. But like the adder in Le Morte d'Arthur, nobody can know how it would have turned out - least of all the Unchained.<br /> <br /> Reading about the Able Archer incident we get a glimpse of the opposite side of this sort of moment in history. In that case, one man saw the proverbial adder at his ankles and made a conscious decision to let it bite him because he knew that if he drew his sword it would mean war. History often unfolds this way - a combination of large scale pressures, individual actions, and freak accidents. Throwing in a Machine that occasionally nudges events in small ways to achieve Its inscrutable goals without regard for its effects on human history just adds one more force of Nature to a world that already has plenty of them playing merry havoc on the &quot;predictable&quot; outcomes of history.<br /> <br /> As has already been said, anything we wrote that included a reference to the Holocaust - however appropriate to the era in question - was likely to touch a nerve. I've been to Auschwitz, but I won't even pretend to have the first fucking idea what it must have been like to been there when it was active. You can't have post-war Berlin without references to war, and you can't have references to that war without at least acknowledging the shadow of the terrible events that happened during it. I wanted to have some tenuous link between the Loyalists of Thule and the Unchained (because they're a great Compact), but I tried not to belabor it or reduce it to something as insulting as &quot;the God-Machine made them do it.&quot; I hope I have not failed in that too badly, and if I have, I'm deeply sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T00:56:23-08:00","id":388121,"title":"","content":"The main thing that's niggling at me \u2014 and this could just be tired nerves fraying my ability to research effectively \u2014 is that 1933 seems almost too late in the game for the misunderstanding to have even the level of impact that it's implied to have had, unless events unfolded very rapidly in the inaugural year of the Third Reich. Am I missing a key something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T03:31:20-08:00","id":388240,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the chapter. I was looking forward to anything that was more Demon, but this was really really good. There's so much included in the timeline as it slumps towards the ultimate destruction of the wall, so many little hints and nudges and flat out interesting things. The story hooks that spin off from it were also really interesting.<br /> <br /> As to the Thule link; I think its a tweaking of a chain in a huge line of events that would have happened anyway. The Loyalists are ashamed of what their actions caused to happen, but would their abscence really have changed all that much? Are the Demons of Berlin just exagerrating the responsibility of the God-Machine? Is a Fall over that even for the objective truth of events. It's kind of like with The Blooded; not all of them are bound to have been War Criminals, but the aura of having survived and profited from the war taints them in the eyes of others (validly, or by sheer jealously.)<br /> <br /> Personally the notion of the God-Machine understanding population dynamics and political swing, but not understanding something as banal and personal as human hatred, fits with the establishment- in much the same way as it only sees Istanbul as a pivot point between two continents, and wants to keep that under control. Ultimately its a system that can't be malicious, not truly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T04:35:16-08:00","id":388316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Satchel:</b> The main thing that's niggling at me \u2014 and this could just be tired nerves fraying my ability to research effectively \u2014 is that 1933 seems almost too late in the game for the misunderstanding to have even the level of impact that it's implied to have had, unless events unfolded very rapidly in the inaugural year of the Third Reich. </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, 1934 is when the Nazi party started suppressing most occult and secret societies (except for Himmler's favourites of course). Which means, if the God-Machine causes a &quot;misunderstanding&quot; in 1933, it could be interpreted as the cause of the Thulists of the time being cast out instead of drafted into the Ahnenerbe, and thus why the Loyalists of Thule became a hunter compact bent on atonement and hatred of Nazis instead of a cult trying to rebuild a Fourth Reich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T15:30:37-08:00","id":388995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=388121#post388121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing that's niggling at me \u2014 and this could just be tired nerves fraying my ability to research effectively \u2014 is that 1933 seems almost too late in the game for the misunderstanding to have even the level of impact that it's implied to have had, unless events unfolded very rapidly in the inaugural year of the Third Reich. Am I missing a key something?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to my (very brief) look into the historical Thule Society there <i>may</i> be a mistake present here (one I think is simply a date issue and shouldn't pose any problem to the narrative at all). Which is to say that the historical Thule Society began to create ties with the DAP (or German Worker's Party) in 1919 which doesn't become the Nazi party until the beginning of 1920. It then fell out of favour and was dissolved sometime around 1925. It did see a resurgence in 1933, but as SunlessNick says, occultism had fallen out of favour with the Nazis and so by 1935 it has dissolved again and its leader is in exile in Turkey.<br /> <br /> At a glance the solution would be simply changing the date of Herr Arger's visitation from 1933 to 1919. I also could have my dates gravely wrong, at which point, keep calm and carry on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T05:36:26-08:00","id":391307,"title":"","content":"1) The black and white portrayal of Eastern Western Berlin and their respected supernatural inhabitants often approaches a puke-inducing level of cWoDs &quot;Berlin by Night&quot;. Calling West Berlin &quot;capitalism paradise&quot; is all good - as long there is a footnote, that it wasn't a &quot;paradise&quot; for quite a lot of people. When the narrative basically goes, that &quot;Eastern Berlin and its masters are meanies, who spy on their citizens, brainwash them, are unjustly paranoid and see threats where there are none, and send spies and saboteurs to the Western Berlin, <b>while</b> the West Berlin and its occupiers do nothing like that&quot; smells like bias.<br /> <br /> How about showing West Berlin\u2019s darker side more prominently, and mention this real-life fact, as the vide employment of former Nazi war criminals by American intelligence services, who often used such agents in East Germany and Eastern Berlin?<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Iron Comrades&quot; made me facepalm myself with severe prejudice. Really? A trashy spy-novel name for psychic-active agents of KGB? Why, do you think that just about everyone in the USSR was obsessed with words &quot;Red&quot; and &quot;Comrade&quot;, and tried to insert them as the names for as many sensetive and top-secret project as was possible? Why there was a destinct lack of such crappy names for the military operations, projects et al during the Great Patriotic War? Why 1944 offensive was codenamed &quot;Bagration&quot;, after, paradoxically, czarist era great general?<br /> <br /> Codename for the first concept of the Soviet hydrogen bomb was not, as many might think, &quot;Hammer &amp; Sickle for Comrades Red Revolution (now with more Balalaikas, Vodka and Russian Bears!)&quot;. No. It was called quite innocently - &quot;<i>Sloyka</i>&quot;, after multi layered puff with different contents.<br /> <br /> Besides - what is this &quot;<u>Red Iron</u> Methode&quot; nonsense?<br /> <br /> And, finally - how one can talk about USSR's psychic experiments and not to mention Stalin's &quot;court magician&quot;, who've became a celebrity even after Stalin's death and was (consiracies, ahoy!) involved in numerous psychic programs, namely - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf_Messing\" target=\"_blank\">Wolf Messing</a>? English-language article on him is outrageusly short, but he is widely known in the former USSR. My grandma was on one of his &quot;seances&quot; in 1950s when she was young.<br /> <br /> 3) Vladimir Yefimovich Semichastny is a real world figure with quite interesting life, who've passed avay relatively recently, in 2001. He was among the conspirators who managed to topple Khruschev in 1964, although he managed to persuade Brazhnev from organising &quot;an accident&quot; for Khruschev, to deal with him permanently.<br /> <br /> And now, we are told that this man knew about vampires? A real life person, head of a real-life intelligence agency, not some comic-book character?<br /> <br /> Correct me, if I'm wrong, but in WoD it is unprecedented for a governmental higher-up to &quot;learn the Truth&quot; and then live happily till the old age? AFAIK, but all &quot;mortal&quot; hunting agencies stress deep secrecy, even if officially they are part of the government. Correct me, if I'm wrong (I'm not so well-versed in NWoD), but no Director of CIA, NSA or FBI in the NWoD USA really knows about the supernatural. Why make A Soviet on counterpart an exception?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T06:12:10-08:00","id":391334,"title":"","content":"It appears we have a Communist apologist over here. <br /> <br /> Let me, an extremely liberal man (with little knowledge of the Cold War, admittedly), show the problems with this art first glance. No offense, but I do consider myself proud of my own country, so let this Yankee offer counterpoints;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391307#post391307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The black and white portrayal of Eastern Western Berlin and their respected supernatural inhabitants often approaches a puke-inducing level of cWoDs &quot;Berlin by Night&quot;. Calling West Berlin &quot;capitalism paradise&quot; is all good - as long there is a footnote, that it wasn't a &quot;paradise&quot; for quite a lot of people. When the narrative basically goes, that &quot;Eastern Berlin and its masters are meanies, who spy on their citizens, brainwash them, are unjustly paranoid and see threats where there are none, and send spies and saboteurs to the Western Berlin, <b>while</b> the West Berlin and its occupiers do nothing like that&quot; smells like bias.<br /> <br /> How about showing West Berlin\u2019s darker side more prominently, and mention this real-life fact, as the vide employment of former Nazi war criminals by American intelligence services, who often used such agents in East Germany and Eastern Berlin?<br /> <br /> <b>And the East Berlin factions are not that much darker. Yes, one Agenda screwed up bad, but it was a good-intentions-paved-road-to-Hell thing (which actually fits, given how those were Integrators). <br /> <br /> Keep in mind the &quot;bias&quot; here was also historical fact; the East Berliners <i>were </i>under a paranoid, intrusive dictatorship, and there are dozens of examples for how that made their citizens do darker things to get the paranoid eye of the Kremlin looking somewhere else. People do not become nice under authoritarians, they close ranks. &quot;Both sides&quot; is never a great criticism, particularly when one built the Wall and their allies stole the Bomb. The tragedy of the setting is good people working for two sides that cannot coexist, and all are capable of heroism and awfulness...but don't pretend Stalin was more of the first than the second.</b><br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Iron Comrades&quot; made me facepalm myself with severe prejudice. Really? A trashy spy-novel name for psychic-active agents of KGB? Why, do you think that just about everyone in the USSR was obsessed with words &quot;Red&quot; and &quot;Comrade&quot;, and tried to insert them as the names for as many sensetive and top-secret project as was possible? Why there was a destinct lack of such crappy names for the military operations, projects et al during the Great Patriotic War? Why 1944 offensive was codenamed &quot;Bagration&quot;, after, paradoxically, czarist era great general?<br /> <br /> <b>Because a lot of the Russians were that silly, it's just that most of their secret project info is still redacted or destroyed. I distinctly recall the perfect worker...<a href=\"http://www.reelz.com/movie-news/15929/stranger-than-fiction-the-soviet-union-tried-to-create-an-army-of-hybrid-ape-men/\" target=\"_blank\">ape-man hybrids</a>. The US had its silly elements too (*cough*Project Stargate*cough*), but I honestly think Soviets would call their psychics something cool, not the least bit to fire up their own patriotism. Or did you think <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicknames_of_United_States_Army_divisions\" target=\"_blank\">these guys</a> are unique to the States?</b><br /> <br /> And, finally - how one can talk about USSR's psychic experiments and not to mention Stalin's &quot;court magician&quot;, who've became a celebrity even after Stalin's death and was (consiracies, ahoy!) involved in numerous psychic programs, namely - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolf_Messing\" target=\"_blank\">Wolf Messing</a>? English-language article on him is outrageusly short, but he is widely known in the former USSR. My grandma was on one of his &quot;seances&quot; in 1950s when she was young.<br /> <br /> <b>Who? Outside the ex-USSR, he's a bit more obscure. This is the first I've heard of him. Thanks for pointing him out, but seriously, we don't know who he is.</b><br /> <br /> 3) Vladimir Yefimovich Semichastny is a real world figure with quite interesting life, who've passed avay relatively recently, in 2001. He was among the conspirators who managed to topple Khruschev in 1964, although he managed to persuade Brazhnev from organising &quot;an accident&quot; for Khruschev, to deal with him permanently.<br /> <br /> And now, we are told that this man knew about vampires? A real life person, head of a real-life intelligence agency, not some comic-book character?<br /> <br /> Correct me, if I'm wrong, but in WoD it is unprecedented for a governmental higher-up to &quot;learn the Truth&quot; and then live happily till the old age? AFAIK, but all &quot;mortal&quot; hunting agencies stress deep secrecy, even if officially they are part of the government. Correct me, if I'm wrong (I'm not so well-versed in NWoD), but no Director of CIA, NSA or FBI in the NWoD USA really knows about the supernatural. Why make A Soviet on counterpart an exception?<br /> <br /> <b>Short answer: No.<br /> <br /> Second answer: Noooooo.<br /> <br /> VALKYRIE has people in the Oval Office and Treasury who know exactly what it is and what it does, while the Barett Commission (Congressional vampire hunters, essentially) continues to exist. It's not hard to imagine Semichantsy being informed of the supernatural elements in his government in the nWoD, and then survivng to live a good long life afterwards. He's not unique.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T07:05:50-08:00","id":391365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears we have a Communist apologist over here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears, that we don't live in McCarty's &quot;Witch Hunt&quot; era, to throw such accusations left and right at anyone who expresses views, with which you may disagree. <br /> <br /> No, I'm not a &quot;Communist apologist&quot;. Also, I've never belong to any left organization or party, and have never vote for such.<br /> <br /> I'm Russian from Russia. Do you have problems with that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the East Berlin factions are not that much darker. Yes, one Agenda screwed up bad, but it was a good-intentions-paved-road-to-Hell thing (which actually fits, given how those were Integrators).</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop strawmaning here. I've never said that that they were &quot;Angels&quot;. It is universal &quot;Dark East vs Light West&quot; presentation that I'm against. More shades of grey, to show, that both sides (and supernaturals in their respective parts of the cities) are not so different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind the &quot;bias&quot; here was also historical fact; the East Berliners <i>were </i>under a paranoid, intrusive dictatorship, and there are dozens of examples for how that made their citizens do darker things to get the paranoid eye of the Kremlin looking somewhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to the veritable &quot;Capitalistic Paradise&quot; in Western Berlin? The first Berlin protests and demonstrations against the occupation happened for the first time in 1947 - in Western Berlin, in British occupation zone. They've began in March and continued for 3 months.<br /> <br /> Or how about to explain more broadly, what kind of &quot;infrastructure&quot; were built here to &quot;<i>cater to a large foreign military population</i>&quot;? All those casinos, bordellos, restaurants - but for occupying troops only.<br /> <br /> Or how about all those NGOs in West Berlin created by then director of the CIA A. Dulles whose aim was real (not imagined by paranoid KGB and Stasi) spying and sabotage in Easter Berlin and East Germany? Don't believe me - check yourself!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People do not become nice under authoritarians, they close ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, are you implying that &quot;under authoritarians&quot; (whatever you understand by this) people, common people, magically transforms into a brainless herd, a horde of violent orks and/or into a trudging masses of morlocks, incapable of positive human feelings, or deriving happiness from the world around them, basically, that they become <i>sub-human</i>, while &quot;under democracy&quot; (again - whatever you understand by this) all people are happy, outgoing and ready to help? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Both sides&quot; is never a great criticism, particularly when one built the Wall and their allies stole the Bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the other side have actually employed said &quot;Bomb&quot;. And have built its foreign policy on threatening with said &quot;Bomb&quot; its enemies or countries, too weak to offer any resistance. I can go with this &quot;whatabautism&quot; for a long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tragedy of the setting is good people working for two sides that cannot coexist, and all are capable of heroism and awfulness...but don't pretend Stalin was more of the first than the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting, actually, take place years after his death. Besides, Stalin =/= the entire USSR, KPSS or the history of the Soviet Union in the XX century.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a lot of the Russians were that silly<b>,</b></div> </div> </div> </div>With silly names from cheap &quot;Red-Scare&quot; era pulp journals? Care to provide real examples?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's just that most of their secret project info is still redacted or destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, this sounds like conspiracy theory - &quot;I can't prove you anything! It was all destroyed or redacted, but you must believe me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I distinctly recall the perfect worker...<a href=\"http://www.reelz.com/movie-news/15929/stranger-than-fiction-the-soviet-union-tried-to-create-an-army-of-hybrid-ape-men/\" target=\"_blank\">ape-man hybrids</a>. </div> </div> </div>That - allegedly - happened in 1920s, even before Stalin consolidated much of the power in his hands. How this one, probably apocryphal incident is an indication of something bigger, is definitely beyond me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The US had its silly elements too (*cough*Project Stargate*cough*), but I honestly think Soviets would call their psychics something cool, not the least bit to fire up their own patriotism. Or did you think <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicknames_of_United_States_Army_divisions\" target=\"_blank\">these guys</a> are unique to the States? </div> </div> </div>Maybe not unique to the States (Google search immediately offered a big list of &quot;Wermacht Divisions Nicknames&quot;), but, I'm absolutely sure, not having any such &quot;analogues&quot; (in the lieu of naming conventions) in the USSR. And this is fact.<br /> <br /> And &quot;Red Comrades&quot; won't &quot;fire up&quot; anyone\u2019s patriotism. Only make everyone facepalm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Short answer: No.<br /> <br /> Second answer: Noooooo.<br /> <br /> VALKYRIE has people in the Oval Office and Treasury who know exactly what it is and what it does, while the Barett Commission (Congressional vampire hunters, essentially) continues to exist. It's not hard to imagine Semichantsy being informed of the supernatural elements in his government in the nWoD, and then survivng to live a good long life afterwards. He's not unique. </div> </div> </div>Okay, let me rephrase it.<br /> <br /> Was there any Western head of the Intelligence service in the NWoD, who'd not only learn about the existence of the supernatural threat, but after his tenure as the head of his Agency, just become an influential regional administrator (Semichantsy was first deputy minister of the Ukrainian SSR from 1967 till 1981) and then retire in comfort, writing memoirs and giving interviews?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T07:26:37-08:00","id":391409,"title":"","content":"I am on a phone right now, so I can't continue the debate at the moment. <br /> <br /> I will say that I am sorry for calling you an apologist: I thought you were American and only realized the mistake later. Defending your country's history isn't something I'm hypocritical enough to mock. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:23:44-08:00","id":391507,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again%E2%80%A6\">Oh, hey.</a><br /> <br /> That's why this seems familiar.<br /> <br /> (Not a plus or a minus)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:41:37-08:00","id":391622,"title":"","content":"It is interesting how perspectives can differ. Without wanting to go too deeply into any debates about the truths of it, my personal impression (as a German, for what it's worth), is that the chapter was exceedingly fair to both sides and tried to keep to facts (ignoring the supernatural bits, obviously) as much as possible. Certainly a far cry from any anti-communist scare-mongering or anything of the sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T11:20:30-08:00","id":391661,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure there are heads of Western intelligence agencies who know about supernatural threats. As Leliel said, <i>Hunter</i> makes this fairly likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-03-2015, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T13:16:59-08:00","id":391782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391365#post391365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was there any Western head of the Intelligence service in the NWoD, who'd not only learn about the existence of the supernatural threat, but after his tenure as the head of his Agency, just become an influential regional administrator (Semichantsy was first deputy minister of the Ukrainian SSR from 1967 till 1981) and then retire in comfort, writing memoirs and giving interviews?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak to everything you've said, and you seem to have some good points, but I think this is something that we do have a pretty clear idea of: Absolutely. Clarified in the 2nd edition materials (and discussed a bit in the <i>Innocents </i>supplement) is the fact that most people in the World of Darkness ignore the supernatural. They might've encountered it once when they were younger or in some other context, they forget about it, they pretend it didn't happen, they ignore it and move on. People that don't do that become Hunters and/or tend to look like crackpot crazy people.<br /> <br /> No Police Officer who wants to keep his badge is going to say that a vampire killed his murder victim. Even if he saw those fangs with his own two eyes, all he'll get is a visit from IA and paid leave to &quot;decompress.&quot; Nobody wants to be 'that guy.' Nevermind the mental trauma of encountering the supernatural for a lot of people (typically represented with Integrity Breaking Points) between stuff like that and the Lie, it's just the nature of the setting. People catch a glimpse of what's real, and they don't go under the bed looking for it. They hide in their covers and try to pretend it doesn't exist. (Protagonists defy this expectation, it's the nature of the story. You might ask, &quot;what if they don't look away?&quot; That's your answer. Those people are the protagonists, the hunters, the monsters themselves, et al.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, to bring it back to your question, I can imagine a regular human being who <i>doesn't </i>want the rest of his life to be hellish, short and maddening going on and ignoring what he might've dealt with when he was doing Intelligence. I'm pretty sure they do that with the mundane intelligence in real life, evident with the real man himself.<br /> <br /> To use an example that demonstrates the principle (I'm not a crazy person!) I'm sure becoming the Prime Minister of &lt;country here&gt; or the President of the United States might entail learning some shocking (albeit, probably not supernatural) secrets about what people are <i>really </i>doing in a lot of murky situations where the rest of us don't know the truth. We don't see these leaders, after they leave office, going off the deep end or blabbing about it, do we?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to leave this as some kind of definitive answer, but I think this is the sort of approach the writers take when seriously considering these kinds of questions. Hope that idea helps your thought process, at least with regards to that question, since I don't think I can help with anything else.<br /> <br /> Lots of people know a lot of secrets about a lot of things, that could totally fuck up their marriage, their home, maybe their neighborhood, city, country, etc. but they manage not to talk about them. The supernatural is just one more in a litany of secrets that people keep. Might even be easier for a former intelligence guy, since that sort of lying was literally his trade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T23:49:45-08:00","id":392416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391661#post391661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure there are heads of Western intelligence agencies who know about supernatural threats. As Leliel said, <i>Hunter</i> makes this fairly likely.</div> </div> </div> </div> And Dogs of War, if Company Zero is a thing (either a company of US military personnel who have templates or supernatural merits, or a group that oversees the US's magic item collection), plus blackfire (?) a pmc that specializes in defending the US's interests against monsters, someone with the authority to write checks to them with the US's piggy banks would have to know what they do.<br /> <br /> In war against the pure there are government agents out to explore exploiting the supernatural for the the benefit of the us government. I want to call them twilight, but I might be thinking about owod there. <br /> <br /> In Falling Scales, the Vice President knows. <br /> <br /> So its safe to say plenty of people in the government know, they just are afraid of upsetting the apple cart....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T04:02:46-08:00","id":392499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391661#post391661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I'm pretty sure there are heads of Western intelligence agencies who know about supernatural threats</b>. As Leliel said, <i>Hunter</i> makes this fairly likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should we treat it like an official &quot;fluff&quot; then, coming from you, as one of the Authors?<br /> <br /> What I really have problem with is all possible cans with worms this can open, and all those questions this inevitably raises:<br /> <br /> 1) Was Semychastniy the first head of KGB to learn about the supernatural? Who else among intelligence agancies knew? Was he the first <i><b>to act</b></i> after gaining this knowledge? Why Berlin? Was Berlin the first city to perform such &quot;Exterminatus&quot; of one particular supernatural type? If it wasn't the first time, then did the Demons assisted mortal agents in previous purges?<br /> <br /> 2) Did his succesor(s) also knew about the supernatural? Semychastniy was succeeded by Andropov, who was head of KGB from 1967 till 1982, when he replaced Leonid Brezhnev as the head of the USSR, till his death in 1984. Gorbachov was close to Andropov circles and his early career was influneced by his patronage. If one head of the state could know, why not another?<br /> <br /> And if we are talking about heads of Intelligence Agencies who could knew the truth and later become heads of the state, what about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_H._W._Bush\" target=\"_blank\">him</a>?<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I'm feeling very uncomfortable with the idea of using real life persons (some - still living) in RPG in such a way. This runs agaunst previously supported concept, that elected officials and others powers that be are deliberately kept in the dark with layers of secrecy, &quot;Need to Know&quot; aproach and &quot;Black Books&quot; financing, offering perfect deniability.<br /> <br /> Another thing I find uncomfortable, is that modern un-American <u>named</u> real-life persons (Adenauer and Semichastniy) were chosen as examples for such &quot;confirmation&quot; - but not from the current or past US administrations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 02-05-2015, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T12:17:49-08:00","id":392849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should we treat it like an official &quot;fluff&quot; then, co,ing from you, as one of the Authors?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a forum post from an author giving a helpful suggestion for your games, if you're so inclined to take it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whay I really have problem with is all possible cans with worms this can open, and all those questions this inevitably raises:</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Edition and books like <i>Tales of the 13th Precinct </i>and <i>Innocents </i>go a long way to address the problem of &quot;people knowing about the supernatural.&quot; When you layer on Integrity and The Lie and Lunacy on top of all those, it doesn't seem particularly liable to add an <i>additional </i>wrinkle. If you dislike the premise of the 2nd edition and books like <i>Innocents </i>then it can't be helped, it's part of the World of Darkness buy-in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Was Semychastniy the first head of KGB to learn about the supernatural? Who else among intelligence agancies knew? Was he the first <i><b>to act</b></i> after gaining this knowledge? Why Berlin? Was Berlin the first city to perform such &quot;Exterminatus&quot; of one particular supernatural type? If it wasn't the first time, then did the Demons assisted mortal agents in previous purges?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably they knew of vampires since he has some kind of vendetta against them in the fiction, obviously they didn't know they were an active thing/issue in Berlin until the start of that plot hook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) 2) Did his succesor(s) also knew about the supernatural? Semychastniy was succeeded by Andropov, who was head of KGB from 1967 till 1982, when he replaced Leonid Brezhnev as the head of the USSR, till his death in 1984. Gorbachov was close to Andropov circles and his early career was influneced by his patronage. If one head of the state could know, why not another?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, given the existence of programs with <i>psychics </i>in them run by the KGB and the Stasi, is it really that surprising? Even the Americans and the British have psychics. The Stasi arrest a sorcerer in 1961. (I feel like I need to clarify that I mean in-setting, not in real life. Duh.)<br /> <br /> In the same vein, if the FBI has Project Wintergreen and V.A.S.C.U. using secret psychic powers to help track down (sometimes) supernatural serial killers, is it really that surprising that the folks in the CIA might have an inkling of the world's hinky, supernatural underbelly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if we are talking about heads of Intelligence Agencies who could knew the truth and later become heads of the state, what about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_H._W._Bush\" target=\"_blank\">him</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure? I don't see how he's relevant, but if you want him to know in your game, go for it. Should I ever feel the need to use George H.W. Bush somehow, I'll do that as well. I mean, he's still alive, and Semichastniy isn't, which is a pretty significant difference when it comes to writing these sorts of historical things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you, but I'm feeling very uncomfortable with the idea of using real life persons (some - still living) in RPG in such a way. This runs agaunst previously supported concept, that elected officials and others powers that be are deliberately kept in the dark with layers of secrecy, &quot;Need to Know&quot; aproach and &quot;Black Books&quot; financing, offering perfect deniability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect deniability is entirely separate from actually not knowing about the supernatural. Again, Demon is a 2nd edition gameline operating on the design principles of the World of Darkness in its second edition. It's more complicated than people just somehow having literally no idea about anything supernatural at any level ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=392499#post392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I find uncomfortable, is that modern un-American <u>named</u> real-life persons (Adenauer and Semichastniy) were chosen as examples for such &quot;confirmation&quot; - but not from the current or past US administrations.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I tried to find his name and it seems like the only mentions of him are in an optional plot idea in the back of the section about him hunting the entirely non-real vampires with the entirely non-real psychic friends. Now that I searched this out, I'm more confused than before about why this is a problem. The only characterization they give you is that he hates vampires. What exactly is the issue with him, beyond using his name? Other figures in history have had their names used in books. See what I wrote below. Adenauer too is basically not characterized here. They just say he's very religious. All he does is tell Rome (and presumably indirectly, the Malleus Maleficarum) that there are demons in Berlin. I don't see how it impugns on either character, particularly given it's all about made-up non-real supernatural monsters.<br /> <br /> If it was an American city and setting about the Red Scare in the States, I'd bet hard money you'd see at least one real person getting namedropped. That's the nature of the beast when you're writing a game that uses <b>history</b>. The difference between a contemporary setting and a historical setting is the desire to explore the character and <i>characters </i>of history. Think Alexander the Great in <i>To The Strongest </i>or Dion O'Banion in <i>Chicago</i>. A more recent example might even be Mother Damnable in <i>Demon</i>. They do this. Writers do this. Dion O'Banion <i>did </i>die in a flower shop, but to my knowledge, he never went on a crusade against &quot;vampires and theosophists&quot; but that's the book fudging the history ever so slightly to generate a plot hook. Which, y'know, is part of the point of using books that research the real history.<br /> <br /> Project VALKYRIE is run by a conspiracy of individuals as an ostensibly government agent. Their leadership could and likely does include heads of intelligence agencies, wealthy business people and potentially even government officials like Senators and the like. And if the heavy-handed hinting that's mentioned practically every time they're discussed that they specifically <i>don't </i>attack certain supernaturals doesn't make it obvious, they're likely corrupt.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you want here. I think your critique of some of the opening's language has a lot of merit. It feels like some of the section is just about Demons navigating everybody in the Cold War, while others seem to frame it like the KGB are THE enemy of the setting, period, which is sorta awkward, since the other parts just address them as part of the landscape of Cold War Berlin.<br /> <br /> Iron Comrades sounds like something Americans or the Unchained might nickname the Russian psychic operatives, rather than their real name. Giving the actual project a more low-key name would be fitting in my opinion, though I don't think you'd need to change everyone else calling them Iron Comrades.<br /> <br /> Like dude, don't stress stuff like &quot;head of CIA knows about werebearcats in alaska&quot; or anything like that. That stuff is either a misunderstanding of the lore or just not really material to your stronger criticisms of the setting. These criticisms seem like a lot of them could be fixed by amending some key sentences here and there, particularly in the introduction. That's good stuff to push for, ideally without being needlessly antagonistic towards the people that could improve the setting with some thoughtful critique.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As an alternative, it could be cool if you would make a separate thread to maybe address your suggestions for how people might homebrew the setting a bit, rather than just spending all the time and energy on saying what's there is bad. I wanna hear about this court magician guy and your ideas on how to tie him into things. I want to hear if you have any cool ideas for what to call the Iron Comrades, in lieu of that name. More content and more options, especially from people that are interested and willing to share their knowledge is always a good thing. Sharing with us some of the bad things that went on in West Berlin just gives us more characterization to work with, and so on. Seriously. You seem to know a lot about it, and if we put that knowledge to positive use rather than just using it to excoriate writers, that could bring some really great added content to the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-04-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T13:13:17-08:00","id":392943,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'm totally cool with George H. W. Bush knowing there are monsters in the World of Darkness. Plenty of people in power know about the monsters. One thing I'd love to do at some point would be a setting where a high-level government task force has to cope with monsters, but doesn't deal with them as its exclusive concern. Not sure exactly what their purview would be, but my fondness for <i>Standalone Complex</i> and <i>Queen and Country</i> would probably shine through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T16:19:59-08:00","id":393168,"title":"","content":"People say 'The Supernatural' like it's some unified bible of truth regarding the way the world works. Of course, in 2e nWoD, heads of state are briefed on a wide variety of totally inexplicable phenomena. This goes far beyond the major templates and probably doesn't even linger particularly long with them. The president hears about the Dero, alien abductions, Nazi moon bases... in the nWoD, he has a stack of papers that's probably two or three feet thick.<br /> <br /> Those that report on these incidents and deal with them are an unreliable lot ; often on the brink of madness or overly involved with various occult conspiracies themselves. Some information is reliable, the vast majority is just 'probably accurate' but 'verifiable and genuine'. The picture painted is not one of a supernatural uber-conspiracy that secretly manipulates humanity, but rather a chaotic storm of Twilight Zone episodes, often devoid of context or greater meaning.<br /> <br /> Which is just how the Machine likes it.<br /> <br /> Every culture hears the signal to some degree, and the modern American culture... much like the Romans, the Greeks, the Egyptians and others before them... hear it reasonably clearly. But only Angels 0truly hear it. What Obama and Bush hear was fuzzy, full of static, and they undoubtedly had very firm opinions on what it meant that were as completely wrong as Pharaohs assumptions. Like every empire that came before, they will believe they hear the Will of God and act on Manifest Destiny. They give specific parts of the signal names and try to do what it wants (or try not to do what it warns them about? Is anybody sure?)<br /> <br /> <br /> Yet one day the signal wanes for all empires! (except, maybe, Irem! Hackers!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T17:25:28-08:00","id":393231,"title":"","content":"Given how much weird shit is in WoD, I can't imagine a lot of intelligence agency people not knowing about supernatural stuff. They would be really bad at their jobs otherwise. The thing is, with so many critters and different sorts of critters, with varying levels of masquerade, for something dedicated to intelligence gathering it would be hard to not stumble over it.<br /> <br /> As noted, though, the Lie and the Integrity stat makes widespread knowledge unlikely. Adding to that, at least in the past century roughly, there has been a pronounced shift in the zeitgeist away from believing in anything which might be considered supernatural. People get mocked for believing in ghosts, much less vampires. For someone famous to stand up and say &quot;Hey guys? Vampires. Also, Werewolves.&quot; in the west would lead to their being roundly mocked and ignored. And outside the west, it is not necessarily gone.<br /> <br /> And honestly, even in the west, many people believe in Angels and Demons. A number believe in ghosts, despite the mockery. None of this has resulted in government actions against Demons.<br /> <br /> So none of it streaches believability for me. What I would find hard to believe, in a world with Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Prometheans, Changelings, Sin-Eaters, Mummies, Demons, Angels, Skinchangers, Immortals, Psychics, and Wookalaars*, if someone invasive as STASI or powerful as the CIA, KGB or FBI had no idea any of that existed.<br /> <br /> Of course, as noted, knowing does not mean accurate or complete information. Believing in Psychics and Demons may still have someone thinking Vampires or Mummies are silly to believe in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*There are totally Wookalaars.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T18:44:47-08:00","id":393294,"title":"","content":"One important thing we say in <i>Vampire </i>is that the Masquerade isn't about quelling belief in the weird, or even in vampires specifically. It's about protecting actual vampires and their society from identification. Demons don't even have a tradition of Masquerade... but disguise comes hardwired, and they've got at least as much to lose as vampires if they're found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T07:21:50-08:00","id":393728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=391334#post391334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I honestly think Soviets would call their psychics something cool, not the least bit to fire up their own patriotism. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to get into the rest of the argument, but from what I understand, the Soviets tended to give their secret projects deliberately bland names. I have no idea what they called their psychic projects, but something like &quot;Research Department 33&quot; would be in keeping. Sometimes it sounds cool by accident though (one of the big facilities developing poisons and ways to deliver them was called &quot;Lab X&quot;).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T10:34:25-08:00","id":393933,"title":"","content":"I have no idea if this is true, but I recall being told that the nazis had an unfortunate tendency to initially give their secret projects significant names that allowed the Allies to guess a lot of what these projects were doing, and from that problem emerged the later idea of naming projects innocuous things to prevent people from guessing what it actually does.<br /> <br /> So it's actually bad idea to give things really obvious names. While iron comrade doesn't scream Psychic all on its own, it implies a project about people, and that's already more specific than is desirable.<br /> <br /> Really, the nature of potential innocuous secret project names can actually make things cooler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T13:42:17-08:00","id":394087,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay.<br /> <br /> I stand corrected. I'm fine with Iron Comrade being a nickname, perhaps even what they call themselves, but realistically it's something akin to Initiative 22 officially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:23:51-08:00","id":394110,"title":"","content":"Iron Comrade is a bit of an old-spy-paperback kind of name, like MI-13. There's probably a secret American program with the words &quot;patriot&quot; or &quot;eagle&quot; in its name. &quot;Homeland&quot; would be a good one for the 2000s. &quot;Union&quot; is taken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T11:56:19-08:00","id":400597,"title":"","content":"Hell, the Pope and the President are in the know. Human society in the nWoD is complicit in the secrecy of the supernatural, for various reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T15:44:13-08:00","id":405223,"title":"","content":"And, to make good on my word, one of the options for the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition/posts/1135264\" target=\"_blank\">next stretch goal</a> is Project Radiant Eagle, America's stigmatic spy initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T18:01:49-08:00","id":406205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/387978-dark-eras-cold-war-berlin?p=393728#post393728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to get into the rest of the argument, but from what I understand, the Soviets tended to give their secret projects deliberately bland names. I have no idea what they called their psychic projects, but something like &quot;Research Department 33&quot; would be in keeping. Sometimes it sounds cool by accident though (one of the big facilities developing poisons and ways to deliver them was called &quot;Lab X&quot;).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Hunter Conspiracy King's Raven and I are working on ( basically Orpheus Projectors if they were KGB) is literally &quot;The Committee for Special Research, Section 21&quot;. Or simply KSI 21.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T18:49:46-08:00","id":406215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-ca